{"title":"2023 WSMO Accuracy Round Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_WSMO_Accuracy_Round_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Bob and his 3 friends are standing in a line of 10 people. Given that Bob is not on either end of the line, then the probability the person in front and behind Bob are both his friends is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f583697295fc6f723862c13228ee55107c33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_WSMO_Accuracy_Round_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The probability the person in front of Bob is his friend is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/d/38d66fd28bf3ba8b51c0aee2face90f6ff78f0c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />. The probability that the person behind Bob is his friend given that the persin in front of Bob is his friend <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/9/33980afecb9562ff64caf9965adfd2045f949de2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />. So, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/a/13a066e0132e023b263cfa00c168f7271d1389cb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\frac{3}{9}\\right)\\left(\\frac28\\right)=\\frac6{72}=\\frac1{12}\\implies1+12 = \\boxed{13}.\\]\" width=\"327\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>~pinkpig\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018024243\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.007 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.008 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 34/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1304/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:31905:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018024243 and revision id 274634. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}